    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the primary statement line 'Total revenues and other income' is composed of three sub-items, which are listed individually. 2. For total_operating_cost, the mapping follows standard practice for the oil & gas industry. It includes all costs of production, manufacturing, selling, general & administrative, depreciation/depletion, exploration, and non-service pension costs. 'Other taxes and duties' and 'Interest expense' are excluded as they are reported separately. 3. 'Other taxes and duties' (26,288 in 2024) is not included in total_operating_cost as it is a separate line item in the 'Costs and other deductions' section and is considered a non-income tax operating expense. Supplementary tables show it includes amounts embedded in production and SG&A expenses, but the primary statement reports it as a distinct line. 4. Net income is mapped to the line attributable to the parent company. 5. Taxes and interest expenses are mapped directly from the primary statement. The sign convention is positive as they reduce income. 6. Supplementary tables for reserves and future cash flows are not directly mapped to income statement line items as they are non-financial operational disclosures.",
